record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-unified-quality-scale-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Search: (1) safe_ceiling_for_rung skips the all-pass ceiling probe when the target sits >=1.5 below the corpus-minimum ceiling of the rung (q50 95.3, q60 96.5, q70 97.4, q75 97.7, q85 98.1, q90 98.3, q92 98.9, q95 99.9), seeding the first aim from the estimate; (2) after a rung wins, a finer rung is tried only with >=3 evaluations left. On 20240502_192515 target 80, Fast now emits the same 107,645 B stream as Balanced in 4 probes with no ceiling probe; 110934 target 80 209,903 B; targets 90: 219,251 / 352,381 B. Unified scale: PerceptualTarget::for_quality(q, effort) defines quality q as a SSIMULACRA2 floor of q (100 stays lossless); CLI accepts 'qN --effort fast|balanced|quality' and routes through it; --ssimulacra2 remains the explicit-score form. Calibration of the legacy open-loop Quality(q) ladder on the eight 0.8 MP corpus photos (ssimulacra2-jpxl-1, median): q10 -63.9, q30 -49.5, q50 -8.8, q60 13.4, q70 35.7, q80 52.3, q90 60.8, q95 79.7 (1.6 bpp), q99 100 (20 bpp). The legacy ladder is therefore not on the unified scale: it is far coarser than the perceptual path below q95 (perceptual score 80 needs a median 1.5 bpp, Quality(80) spends 0.77 bpp) and jumps 12x in bytes between q95 and q99. Re-pointing Quality(q) at the unified scale (bpp prior per target from the sweep: t80 1.52, t85 1.96, t90 2.60, t95 4.26, t97.5 7.08 median bpp) changes every consumer's file sizes and is left for an explicit decision. 4-6 MP calibration run still in flight at record time. Lib 375/375 serial, all integration targets and CLI unit tests green."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 && cargo test --no-fail-fast --test '*' && cargo test --features cli --bin jp2lam && target/release/examples/perceptual_curve test-set 10,20,30,40,50,60,70,75,80,85,90,95,99"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/src/model.rs"
    summary """
        Search: (1) safe_ceiling_for_rung skips the all-pass ceiling probe when the target sits >=1.5 below the corpus-minimum ceiling of the rung (q50 95.3, q60 96.5, q70 97.4, q75 97.7, q85 98.1, q90 98.3, q92 98.9, q95 99.9), seeding the first aim from the estimate; (2) after a rung wins, a finer rung is tried only with >=3 evaluations left. On 20240502_192515 target 80, Fast now emits the same 107,645 B stream as Balanced in 4 probes with no ceiling probe; 110934 target 80 209,903 B; targets 90: 219,251 / 352,381 B. Unified scale: PerceptualTarget::for_quality(q, effort) defines quality q as a SSIMULACRA2 floor of q (100 stays lossless); CLI accepts 'qN --effort fast|balanced|quality' and routes through it; --ssimulacra2 remains the explicit-score form. Calibration of the legacy open-loop Quality(q) ladder on the eight 0.8 MP corpus photos (ssimulacra2-jpxl-1, median): q10 -63.9, q30 -49.5, q50 -8.8, q60 13.4, q70 35.7, q80 52.3, q90 60.8, q95 79.7 (1.6 bpp), q99 100 (20 bpp). The legacy ladder is therefore not on the unified scale: it is far coarser than the perceptual path below q95 (perceptual score 80 needs a median 1.5 bpp, Quality(80) spends 0.77 bpp) and jumps 12x in bytes between q95 and q99. Re-pointing Quality(q) at the unified scale (bpp prior per target from the sweep: t80 1.52, t85 1.96, t90 2.60, t95 4.26, t97.5 7.08 median bpp) changes every consumer's file sizes and is left for an explicit decision. 4-6 MP calibration run still in flight at record time. Lib 375/375 serial, all integration targets and CLI unit tests green.
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.jp2lam-verified-quality-api-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Implements lege-ecosystem.decision.jp2lam-verified-quality-scale. API: RateControl::Quality { level, effort } (verified SSIMULACRA2 floor = level), RateControl::ApproxQuality(u8) (legacy open-loop preset, behaviour unchanged), RateControl::Perceptual (expert raw score), EncodeOptions::photo_quality(level); EncodeOptions::photo and the photo presets are verified/balanced; EncodeOptions.quality field documented as the approximate preset. CLI: qN [--effort] = verified, --approx qN = legacy, auto classifier = legacy, --ssimulacra2 = expert. Controller: first probe seeded from the corpus bpp prior (prior_bpp_for_score: t80 1.52, t90 2.60, t95 4.26 bpp), loss-model shrink after a feasible probe, ACCEPT_OVERSHOOT 0.5 stops once within half a point above target, MIN_BRACKET_STEP escalates per consecutive infeasible probe (flat plateaus under target). Probe counts on two 0.8 MP photos: q80 fast 3/4, balanced 5/4; q90 fast 4/3, balanced 5/6. Bytes: 192515 q80 105,697 (fast) / 103,922 (balanced), q90 215,984 both; 110934 q80 206,833 both, q90 342,322 both; Fast now matches Balanced bytes on 3 of 4 pairs. Lib 376/376 serial, all integration targets, CLI 10/10, all targets build. No workspace consumer used RateControl::Quality; consumers set only the EncodeOptions.quality field, whose output is unchanged."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 && cargo test --no-fail-fast --test '*' && cargo test --features cli --bin jp2lam && cargo build --features cli --all-targets && target/release/jp2lam encode test-set/{20240502_192515,20240501_110934}.png q{80,90} --effort {fast,balanced}"
    artifact "lege-codecs/jp2lam/src/model.rs"
    summary """
        Implements lege-ecosystem.decision.jp2lam-verified-quality-scale. API: RateControl::Quality { level, effort } (verified SSIMULACRA2 floor = level), RateControl::ApproxQuality(u8) (legacy open-loop preset, behaviour unchanged), RateControl::Perceptual (expert raw score), EncodeOptions::photo_quality(level); EncodeOptions::photo and the photo presets are verified/balanced; EncodeOptions.quality field documented as the approximate preset. CLI: qN [--effort] = verified, --approx qN = legacy, auto classifier = legacy, --ssimulacra2 = expert. Controller: first probe seeded from the corpus bpp prior (prior_bpp_for_score: t80 1.52, t90 2.60, t95 4.26 bpp), loss-model shrink after a feasible probe, ACCEPT_OVERSHOOT 0.5 stops once within half a point above target, MIN_BRACKET_STEP escalates per consecutive infeasible probe (flat plateaus under target). Probe counts on two 0.8 MP photos: q80 fast 3/4, balanced 5/4; q90 fast 4/3, balanced 5/6. Bytes: 192515 q80 105,697 (fast) / 103,922 (balanced), q90 215,984 both; 110934 q80 206,833 both, q90 342,322 both; Fast now matches Balanced bytes on 3 of 4 pairs. Lib 376/376 serial, all integration targets, CLI 10/10, all targets build. No workspace consumer used RateControl::Quality; consumers set only the EncodeOptions.quality field, whose output is unchanged.
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.lege-process-display-preset-integration-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Opus subagent, lege-process. Flow: page rasters are Lanczos-resized to the device preset before region cropping (pdf_tokio_pipeline.rs ~686-760), so region pixel size is the device placement box; PDF placement (pdf_artifact.rs CTM) is decoupled from XObject pixel size. New EncodingSettings::Jp2Display { max_width, max_height, floor, fallback_quality } with or_legacy(): verified display target (jp2lam EncodeOptions::display_photo with DisplayProfile eink/tablet by channel count, resampling_source) only when the source is meaningfully larger than the box, legacy ApproxQuality preset otherwise. quality_policy floors: region 78/75/70, gray overlay 70/65, full-page base 60/55 (65 measured +3..52% bytes there). All five JP2 sites declare a box; preserved-MRC path untouched. --jp2-debug rewritten to compare legacy vs floor with reader-visible SSIMULACRA2. Real 2663x4506 book-scan pages into 709x1200 e-ink box: bytes 0.68x, encode 0.38x, decode 0.23x, score equal or better. Box == source (472x800 crops): the 1+1 display controller overshoots 10-25 points at 1.1-2.0x bytes vs legacy, hence or_legacy; forwarded to the navigation agent. Gates: cargo check -p lege ok, cargo test -p lege 339+19 passed, jp2lam untouched. Remaining upstream win: encode regions from the pre-resize raster so jp2lam does the downscale inside the rate loop (pipeline restructure)."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "cargo check -p lege --all-targets && cargo test -p lege && lege <pdf> <pages> --jp2-debug 2400"
    artifact "lege-process/encoding/streamline.rs"
    summary """
        Opus subagent, lege-process. Flow: page rasters are Lanczos-resized to the device preset before region cropping (pdf_tokio_pipeline.rs ~686-760), so region pixel size is the device placement box; PDF placement (pdf_artifact.rs CTM) is decoupled from XObject pixel size. New EncodingSettings::Jp2Display { max_width, max_height, floor, fallback_quality } with or_legacy(): verified display target (jp2lam EncodeOptions::display_photo with DisplayProfile eink/tablet by channel count, resampling_source) only when the source is meaningfully larger than the box, legacy ApproxQuality preset otherwise. quality_policy floors: region 78/75/70, gray overlay 70/65, full-page base 60/55 (65 measured +3..52% bytes there). All five JP2 sites declare a box; preserved-MRC path untouched. --jp2-debug rewritten to compare legacy vs floor with reader-visible SSIMULACRA2. Real 2663x4506 book-scan pages into 709x1200 e-ink box: bytes 0.68x, encode 0.38x, decode 0.23x, score equal or better. Box == source (472x800 crops): the 1+1 display controller overshoots 10-25 points at 1.1-2.0x bytes vs legacy, hence or_legacy; forwarded to the navigation agent. Gates: cargo check -p lege ok, cargo test -p lege 339+19 passed, jp2lam untouched. Remaining upstream win: encode regions from the pre-resize raster so jp2lam does the downscale inside the rate loop (pipeline restructure).
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.encode-quality.evidence.lege-verified-regions-and-2x-render-2026-09-05/1 : evidence {
    title "Round 5 (no subagents): or_legacy removed and JP2 regions rendered 2x for in-loop downscale. Finding: the product renders pages AT device height (source_render_height == target_height unless slow OCR) and the planned path renders region products at crop size, so box == source is the common case and or_legacy sent nearly every JP2 region to legacy q50, which measured SSIMULACRA2 -25..42 on 21 device-resolution Central Park figure crops (median ~10). jp2lam root cause at box == source: the display policy (2-probe cap, display reserve) applied to a profile that conditions nothing; on the crops it shipped fat first probes (floor 55 landed 65-82 at up to 1.56x plain bytes). Fix: DisplayProfile::conditions(); prepared_context plans an identity profile as the plain target (resampled encodes keep theirs to condition the original reference). Crops now byte-identical to plain (21/21). lege-process: or_legacy deleted, every JP2 site verified (fallback_quality kept for encode failure only); slow-OCR hi-res raster crops feed JP2 regions/cover with the device box; planned path renders JP2 regions at JP2_REGION_RENDER_SCALE=2 so jp2lam box-filters in linear light inside the rate loop. Central Park p20-40: JPX bytes legacy 403K -> verified 965K (floor 55 vs q50, quality-level change) -> 2x render 823K (0.85x) at equal verified score; wall 3.6 s -> 4.8 s for 21 pages. Page-level jp2-debug 2800 vs 1400 render into the 1400 box: 0.85-0.90x bytes, score delta within +-1.5, encode ms 1.24-1.52x. Gates: jp2lam fmt clean, all-targets 0 warnings, lib 381 serial, integration all green (perceptual_api 13 incl. identity test), CLI 12; lege fmt, check, test 341+19 (new slow_ocr_jp2_region test)."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command "lege cp.pdf 20-40 (legacy / verified / 2x builds, JPX stream totals); jp2lam encode crops/*.png --ssimulacra2 55 vs 55 --display tablet:WxH vs crops2x --resample, scored with examples/score_stream; cargo test -p lege; jp2lam gate set"
    artifact "lege-process/pipeline/page_output_plan.rs"
    summary """
        or_legacy removed (regions were legacy q50 at box == source, SSIM -25..42); identity display profiles planned as plain targets (byte-identical, up to 1.56x saved on stranded crops); JP2 regions rendered at 2x so jp2lam downscales in linear light in the rate loop: 0.85x region bytes at equal verified score for +33% wall on a photo book.
        """
}

