    command "cargo test --profile debug-fast -p lege --lib; cargo test --profile debug-fast -p pdf-render-cpu; cargo test --profile debug-fast -p lege-pdf-read; bash lege-misc/dev-misc/warncheck.sh; target/debug-fast/lege <Gobineau> 40-59 [--text-format glyphfont] --no-ocr --debug-runtime-stats; target/debug-fast/lege <Gobineau> 40-42 --text-format glyphfont --ocr; target/debug-fast/lege <Hurvitz> 60-62 --text-format glyphfont --ocr"
    summary """
        lege lib 317 passed / 1 ignored; pdf-render-cpu and lege-pdf-read suites green including the new gray-vs-RGB twin and area-average tests; warncheck PASS across the matrix. Gobineau pages 40-59 (machine quiet, load 1.5): glyphfont 14.9 s wall / 66 s CPU -> 4.3 s / 18 s, JBIG2 mode 6.6 s / 26 s -> 3.3 s / 13 s; per-stage CPU: output render 22.7 -> 3.0 s, analysis render 6.2 -> 2.3 s, preserved-mask probe 5.9 -> 1.7 s, encode 13.2 -> 4.0 s; shared image cache 0 -> 20 hits. Sizes: glyphfont 20 pages 342 KB -> 183 KB, JBIG2 617 KB -> 378 KB with visibly cleaner letter edges (crop compared by eye). Pages 40-42 with OCR: word recall 0.833 / 0.853 / 0.853 over three runs (precision 0.803-0.816), inside the run-to-run band. Hurvitz sideways spread 60-62: glyphfont 438 KB, 1098 / 1127 / 1068 extracted words; JBIG2 152 KB unchanged (not a preserved-mask source). Review copies in ~/Downloads/lege-review-2026-09-03/.
        """
}

record lege-ecosystem.evidence.glyphfont-speck-filter-crusades-20260906/1 : evidence {
    title "Dropping isolated specks before glyph matching removes 18 percent of occurrences and 7 percent of bytes on the crusades scan"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:df6bb8cf45e9ee68a6544bbaf9e9136f6cd171d2
    command """
        lege book.pdf 1-41 --text-format truetyping (crusadeswholesto0000lamb_1.pdf, debug-logging build, 2026-09-06)
        """
    summary """
        PageAnalysis::of now drops a component that is grain: at most dpi^2/24000 ink pixels anywhere (2 at 240 dpi, cjb2's own 3 at 300), or at most dpi^2/4800 pixels (12 at 240) when it is no more than a quarter the page's upper-quartile component side and has no other ink within dpi/20 pixels of its box. Before: 224855 occurrences, 13087 shapes, 2.17 MB font, 2.56 MB PDF, 14.7 s. After: 184452 occurrences, 40403 specks dropped, 13060 shapes, 2.12 MB font, 2.38 MB PDF, 10.4 s. Full stops and tittles survive on page 20. The one-off shapes that dominate the font are not specks: of 11122 shapes used once, 5164 are letter-sized (17-64 px) unmatched impressions and 5782 are 4-16 px fragments, against 472 reused letter-sized prototypes.
        """
    derived_from [
        @lege-ecosystem.observation.grayscale-mode-makes-truetyping-smaller-and-cleaner
    ]
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

